.Language=English,English
.PluginContents=Backup Editor files v1.0

@Contents
$ #Backup Editor files v1.0#
    This plugin allows to create backup (BAK) files when you save files in internal editor.

    In editor you can enable creation of backup copies only for current editor session
by selecting corresponding item in editor plugin menu. This makes sense if you switched off
always to create backup copies.

    In configuration dialog you may change the following options:

 #Create BAK files#         If this option is on, plugin will create
                          BAK files.

 #Create B00, B01, ...#     If this option is on, plugin will create
 #files#                    new (non existing) file and won't overwrite
                          existing BAK file.

 #Create only one copy#     If this option is on, copy will be created
 #in session#               when file is saved first time only. That is
                          during one session of editor only one copy will
                          be created independent of number of times you
                          saved the file.

 #Create a copy at#         If this option is on, when editor starts,
 #editor start#             plugin creates a copy.

 #Append .bak to#           If this option is on, file backup copy will be
 #file name#                <filename.ext.bak> rather than <filename.bak>

 #Don't create copies#      When you edit a file in archive FAR create it
 #in archives#              in temp directory. If you don't want to create
                          copy in this directory, select the option.

 #Don't change#             You can enable this option only if 
 #file name#                #Use specified backup folder# is on. In such a
                          case plugin will create copies in specified folder
                          without changing file names.

 #Use specified#            If this option is on, plugin will create
 #backup folder#            copies in specified folder, rather than
                          in folder where file is located.
